    "https://careers.miami.edu/us/en/residency-program": {
      "title": "Launch Your Nursing Career with Confidence",
      "description": "Residency Program | University of Miami Titan Canes Nurse Residency Program With strong leadership, innovative learning tools, and a commitment to professional development, UHealth is where your nursing journey begins with purpose and pride. Explore Careers REGISTERED NURSE RESIDENCY PROGRAM  2027 SPRING, SUMMER AND FALL - March, July and October RN Residency Interest List APPLY HERE Med Surgical Telemetry, Oncology, Surgical Oncology, Urology, Neurology, Neurology Surgery, Cardiothoracic Step Down, PCU, Head and Neck, IMCU & More Launch Your Nursing Career with Confidence at UHealth UHealth’s Titan Canes Nurse Residency Program has earned accreditation from the American Nurses Credentialing Center’s Commission in Practice Transition Programs (PTAP)—a symbol of excellence shared by only a select group of health care institutions worldwide. Designed to support new nurse graduates as they transition into clinical practice, the program offers a structured, supportive environment across specialties including surgical, oncology, critical care, and ambulatory care. What to Expect from Your Titan ‘Canes Residency Experience We believe that behind every confident, successful nurse is a solid foundation of unparalleled training and support. Through our Nurse Residency Program, you’ll build the advanced skills and competencies needed to enhance your transition into clinical practice with ongoing mentorship from nursing staff, leaders and academic experts. Our 12-month program, in partnership with HealthStream Jane AI and Vizient/AACN Nurse Residency programs, offers you the opportunity to: Grow your professional leadership and emotional intelligence skill Deliver high-quality patient care Advance your empathetic listening and communication Contribute to the advancement of health care through research and quality improvement projects Access continuing education courses, resources and most up-to-date health information Program Information Orientation to the University of Miami Hospital and Clinics (UMHC) system, nursing department, standards of care, and clinical skills Didactic lectures covering UMHC’s Policies and Core Competencies, based on specialty curriculum 14 to 18 weeks of unit-based training with a qualified preceptor and Clinical Educator Monthly education sessions that address leadership, patient outcomes, and professionalism Eligibility Requirements Graduate from accredited school of nursing Bachelor’s in nursing (BSN) preferred* *RNs hired with an (ASN) will have 2 years to complete the BSN degree Valid Florida RN License BLS & ACLS certifications from the American Heart Association Less than 12 months of full-time RN experience by hire date Application Process The Titan Canes Residency Program runs three cohorts each year: around March, July, and October . Applications open one month in advance and remain active for one week. Join our Talent Community to be notified when the next application window opens. Join Our Talent Community Our Care Settings UHealth offers nurse residencies in various practice settings and specialties that fit your interests and career goals, including: ​​ Inpatient - UHealth Tower Medical-Surgical (Med-Surg) Orthopedics and Neurosurgery Stepdown Neurology Cardiothoracic Stepdown Surgical Urology Cardiac Telemetry Head and Neck Intensive Care Units (ICU) Intermediate Care Units Oncology Progressive Care Unit Respiratory Stepdown Emergency Department Ambulatory Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center The Lennar Foundation Medical Center UHealth Doral SoLè Mia Launch Your Career with UHealth – Apply Today! For more information about our student nurse intern, residency or fellowship programs, contact us today at utalent@miami.edu . 7348f6c2da34495c84f60ecbf7f3792f"
    },
    "https://careers.miami.edu/us/en/job-fairs": {
      "title": "Helping you to find your new purpose",
      "description": "Job Fairs | University of Miami Job Fairs It's time to invest in you! Explore Careers The University of Miami is a vibrant community focused on education and learning, the discovery of new knowledge, and service to the South Florida region and beyond. We foster a collaborative environment where faculty and staff feel valued and have the opportunity to add value, making the U a great place to pursue your passions and grow your career. We host in-person and virtual job fairs throughout the year. Participate and transform lives. Use these events to: Meet with recruiters Meet with hiring managers Learn more about the application process/timelines Discover new career possibilities and development opportunities. Helping you to find your new purpose 30c779f83c10496ba040965fcd411cd2"
    },
